## Goal
Clarify ADR 0007 (notification on a failed "Remember") so it states what happens to a pending notification on an explicit quit such as logout or Quit (DEV-50).

## Problems
None.

## Decision
The ADR text in `docs/adr/0007-remember-failure-notification.md` was edited in two ways:
- The in-flight wording now says the pending permission prompt or delivery blocks only the idle quit, not every quit.
- A new sentence states that an explicit quit keeps its existing 10 s cap in `applicationShouldTerminate` (handler.m). A logout should not wait up to a minute for a banner, so a notification still pending then is dropped. This is safe because the link is already open and the log line is already written (decision 5).

The ADR records the behaviour so the 60 s and 5 s waits are not mistaken for a delay on quit. Only documentation changed; no code.

